<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42321" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sălictārĭus</span></b> ,
			a, um
		id.. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			Adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to willows</i>, <i>willow-</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lupus,</span>”
				<i>a kind of wild hop that grows in willowgrounds</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					21, 15, 50, § 86</span></i>
			.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sălictārĭus</span></b> ,
			ii, m., <i>one who takes care
				of willow-trees</i>, <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 11,
			1</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
